  "critique": {
    "axis": "aesthetics",
    "evidence": "The screen has a cohesive, polished command-console aesthetic: disciplined cyan/green/yellow accents, strong headline typography, consistent borders and badges, and clear BLOCK→ALLOW storytelling. However, desktop composition leaves excessive empty space around the hero and separates the results explanation awkwardly to the right. Tablet becomes very tall and repetitive, while mobile metadata is extremely small and the precedent rows lose the desktop’s compact comparative rhythm. The global header also visibly truncates navigation at desktop/mobile widths, making the chrome feel unfinished.",
    "fix": "Tighten the desktop hero into a more balanced grid, compress tablet/mobile row spacing, raise the smallest metadata type size and contrast, and redesign the header’s responsive navigation so labels never appear partially clipped.",
